{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception interface, separating physical actions from sensor outcomes. The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: forward/random_walk in clear, conservative recovery on obstacles, and rapid return to exploration. Recovery states are one-shot, and backward motion is used only for front-obstacle recovery. All uncontrollable events are handled in every state, and only one controllable is enabled per action state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion (controllable) and perception (uncontrollable) to reflect the robot's interface.",
    "Specification automaton binds perception outcomes to allowed actions, enforcing safe, coverage-biased exploration and conservative recovery."
  ],
